6059198 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059198 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059198 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e1747404-bda2-554f-9efe-0485e7c51625" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059199 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059199 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059199 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ff8c7d79-b462-5853-a89f-67185424d9cd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059200 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\sqrt{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059200 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059200 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "089e0d84-9527-5be5-b758-b27167f17812" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059201 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059201 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059201 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5f2e74fd-f5d4-5202-b322-27b3f5c0dc39" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059399 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12613" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059399 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the value of $\\cos 225^\\circ$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059399 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ce1e1013-987e-5c1e-82e6-a8524d8be168" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059399 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's remind ourselves of the special trigonometric ratios, as given by the unit circle.\n\n![](images/d9/d93c490adbb5cdbc0e9a09b60eea9b82ab93be8e871e334423abc17ddd62955e.png)\n\nFrom the unit circle, we see that the angle $225^\\circ$ corresponds to the point\n\n$$\n\\left(-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}, -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\right)\n$$\n\nSince the cosine of the angle corresponds to the $x$-coordinate, we have\n\n$$\n\\cos 225^\\circ = -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059400 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12614" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059400 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the value of $\\sin \\left(\\dfrac {7\\pi} 4\\right)$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059400 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "dd543c7f-fb05-54a9-a9e3-3f7cb88940b9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059400 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's remind ourselves of the special trigonometric ratios, as given by the unit circle.\n\n![](images/db/dbf36192ac332dc49ed75278838e989a37ac7d888311be1b8b059a7b59667aa6.png)\n\nFrom the unit circle, we see that the angle\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{7\\pi}{4}\n$$\n\ncorresponds to the point\n\n$$\n\\left(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}, -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\right)\n$$\n\nSince the sine of the angle corresponds to the $y$-coordinate, we have\n\n$$\n\\sin \\left(\\dfrac {7\\pi} 4\\right) = -\\dfrac {\\sqrt 2} 2\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059401 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12615" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059401 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the value of $\\csc 120^\\circ$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059401 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "179c218a-924a-57a6-93fd-44899242412f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059401 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's remind ourselves of the special trigonometric ratios, as given by the unit circle.\n\n![](images/d9/d93c490adbb5cdbc0e9a09b60eea9b82ab93be8e871e334423abc17ddd62955e.png)\n\nFrom the unit circle, we see that the angle $120^\\circ$ corresponds to the point\n\n$$\n\\left(-\\dfrac{1}{2}, \\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\right)\n$$\n\nSince the sine of the angle corresponds to the $y$-coordinate, we have\n\n$$\n\\sin 120^\\circ= \\dfrac{\\sqrt 3}{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the fact that\n\n$$\n\\csc{\\theta} = \\dfrac{1}{\\sin\\theta}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\csc 120^\\circ = \\dfrac{1}{\\sin 120^\\circ} = \\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt 3} = \\dfrac{2\\sqrt 3}{3}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059402 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12616" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059402 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the value of $\\tan \\left(\\dfrac {4 \\pi} 3\\right)$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059402 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "41928771-a3e4-54fb-9237-e60191f215c1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059402 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's remind ourselves of the special trigonometric ratios, as given by the unit circle.\n\n![](images/db/dbf36192ac332dc49ed75278838e989a37ac7d888311be1b8b059a7b59667aa6.png)\n\nFrom the unit circle, we see that the angle\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4\\pi}{3}\n$$\n\ncorresponds to the point\n\n$$\n\\left(-\\dfrac{1}{2}, -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\right)\n$$\n\n- Since the cosine of the angle corresponds to the $x$-coordinate, we have $\\cos\\left(\\dfrac {4\\pi} {3}\\right) = -\\dfrac 1 2$.\n- Since the sine of the angle corresponds to the $y$-coordinate, we have $\\sin\\left(\\dfrac {4\\pi} {3}\\right) = -\\dfrac {\\sqrt 3} 2$.\n\nTherefore, using the fact that\n\n$$\n\\tan{\\theta} = \\dfrac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\tan\\left(\\dfrac{4\\pi}{3}\\right) = \\dfrac{\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{4\\pi}{3}\\right)}}{\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{4\\pi}{3}\\right)}} = \\dfrac{\\left(-\\dfrac {\\sqrt 3} 2\\right)}{\\left(-\\dfrac 1 2\\right)} = \\sqrt{3}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059843 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050103 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059843 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050847 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059843 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186051043 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059843 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186060222 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059843 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186060223 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059843 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233307 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059843 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233308 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059843 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186234461 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059843 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186234462 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059843 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186570015 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059843 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Sine or Cosine of a Special Angle Given in Degrees" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059843 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186059399 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059843 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "6699397d-0014-5749-b439-4a8486990986" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059